    "proposed_facts": [
      {
        "index": 0,
        "supported": true,
        "reason": "Independently read all three cited canonical excerpts. DownSpot animation completion calls the orientation-selecting DownWait initializer, which initializes x0; DownWait suppresses decrement while x2224_b2 is set. The defeat dispatcher sets that flag and sends its non-air branch to DownSpot. The proposal and functionality document agree and do not assert that DownWait can never exit: the <=0 check remains outside the decrement guard. Existing callback names and supported retained knowledge require no overrides."
      }
    ],
